
# nr-office-pdf-jbig2-generic: mixdog-pdf gets src/codec (the MQ arithmetic decoder, JBIG2 generic / refinement regions and page composition, CCITT G3/G4), written and checked; the module line, two dev-dependencies and a notice line are the lead's.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/lib.rs: declare the module (after `pub mod codec_glue;`)
    pub mod codec;
(`src/codec/mod.rs` declares `arith`, `ccitt` and `jbig2`; nothing else of the crate refers to it yet.)

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/Cargo.toml, [dev-dependencies]: add (the twin test `tests/twin_jbig2_generic.rs`)
    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }
    mixdog-testkit = { workspace = true }
Both are `[workspace.dependencies]` entries already. No new external crate: the decoders use only `std`.
No edge from mixdog-office-base or mixdog-testkit back to mixdog-pdf (no cycle).

## 3. native/core/Cargo.lock: the `mixdog-pdf` package entry gains two dependencies (alphabetical)
    "mixdog-office-base",
    "mixdog-testkit",
(`cargo metadata --offline --locked` rewrites it the same way.)

## 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/NOTICE: add, after the pdf.js paragraph
    The JBIG2 and CCITT fax decoders in src/codec (arith.rs, ccitt.rs, jbig2/) are ported from PDFium's
    core/fxcodec/jbig2 and core/fxcodec/fax, the code pdf.js 6.4.299 ships as wasm/jbig2.wasm, which is
    licensed under the BSD 3-Clause licence: Copyright 2014 The PDFium Authors (the licence text is
    wasm/LICENSE_JBIG2 of pdfjs-dist), redistributed under its terms. The T.4 run-length code tables in
    ccitt.rs are the standard's.

