## 5. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack, hakari, SERVICE_PENDING, protocol rows
Nothing: no service, no method, no new dependency of mixdog-pdf at run time.

## 6. What later tasks consume (interfaces added, all `pub` under `mixdog_pdf::codec`)
- `codec::jbig2::decode(data, width: i32, height: i32, globals: Option<&[u8]>) -> Result<Vec<u8>, CodecError>`
  and `codec::jbig2::strip_file_header(bytes)` (pdf.js `Jbig2Stream.stripFileHeader`: the caller strips the file header of
  the image stream and of the `JBIG2Globals` stream, then calls `decode` with the image dictionary's `Width` and `Height`
  as `codec::to_int32` of the number; the output is the packed 1-bit rows, 0 = black, `(width + 7) / 8` bytes each, the
  buffer pdf.js's `Jbig2Stream` returns).
- `codec::ccitt::decode(data, width: i32, height: i32, &CcittParams) -> Result<Vec<u8>, CodecError>`; `CcittParams` has
  pdf.js 6.4's `CCITTFaxStream` defaults (`K` 0, `Columns` 1728 when 0 or absent, `Rows` 0) in `Default`; the caller fills it
  from `/DecodeParms` as `CCITTFaxStream`'s constructor does, `K` and `Columns` and `Rows` through `to_int32`.
- `codec::CodecError` (`Unknown` = "Unknown error", `DivideByZero`, `Message`): `message()` is the exception text of the wrapper.
- For nr-office-pdf-jbig2-symbols (the next task, `huffman.rs symbols.rs text.rs halftone.rs`):
  `codec::arith::{ArithDecoder, ArithCx, ArithIntDecoder (IAx), ArithIaidDecoder}`, `jbig2::image::{Image, ComposeOp}`
  (`get_pixel set_pixel fill copy_line compose_to compose_rows_to sub_image padded_pixel data data_mut stride`),
  `jbig2::generic::GenericRegion` (arithmetic with `skip` and every template, `decode_mmr` for the halftone's bit planes),
  `jbig2::refine::RefinementRegion` (with `dx`/`dy`), `jbig2::{BitStream, Segment, SegmentResult}`.
  That task must also edit `jbig2/mod.rs` (it is this task's file; the task list gives it no file there): replace the arm of
  `Context::parse_data` that fails the segment types 0, 4, 6, 7, 16, 20, 22, 23 and 53 by their parsers, add the `mod`
  lines for its modules and the bit readers (`read_bit`, `read_bits`) its Huffman decoding needs to `BitStream`, and add a
  `SegmentResult` variant for each result it stores (symbol dictionary, pattern dictionary, table). Until it does, a stream
  holding one of those segments fails with "Unknown error".
- For nr-exthost-pdf-document (`codec_glue.rs`): register `JBIG2Decode` and `CCITTFaxDecode` of `StreamFilters` over the
  two functions above (both are decoders of images: pdf.js hands the decoded bytes to the image code unchanged).
